                "post_type": "quote",
                "quote_count": 0,
                "quoted_status_id": "1987685841670480349",
                "quoted_status_profile_id": "1078771848882593793",
                "quoted_status_profile_username": "SenatorAndyKim",
                "reply_count": 34,
                "retweet_count": 50,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Americans across the country are demanding a solution that avoids catastrophic increases to healthcare premiums. Sadly, but not surprisingly, Trump and Congressional Republicans have failed to come to the table. \n\nFrom the beginning, I've said I was ready to work to reopen government and protect the healthcare of my constituents. Point blank, this so called \"deal\" fails that very basic test. \n\nA pinky promise to hold a vote in the Senate (and not even in the House) is not a \"deal,\" It's a failure of leadership. Senate Dems should vote \"Hell no.\"",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
